  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">End Period Poverty in Rural Schools in Malawi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Period poverty means lack of funds to buy basic personal hygiene items: sanitary  pads, soap, underwear, no access to toilets and running water, and no basic knowledge about menstruation. In Malawi many young girls experience period poverty, therefore they don&apos;t go to school during menstruation, which causes dropping out of school and, consequently, the end of education. YORGHAS Foundation aims to help 500 school age girls gain access to menstrual supplies and knowledge on menstrual hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
